VIOLATION — tenant-isolation.md MUST-4. Thirteen metric families each gain a raw `tenant_id` label
with nothing bounding its domain. The clause permits the label only with bounded cardinality and
names two acceptable strategies — top-N bucketing with the remainder under one bucket, or emitting
the full tenant at the log tier and letting the pipeline aggregate. The transcript considers the
first and rejects it, and never reaches the second, so neither bound is in place. It also reproduces
the clause's own arithmetic against itself: 13 families at 10K tenants is the 130K series the rule
names as well past the practical limit, and the session books that as a year of headroom.

The staging measurement is real and is the wrong instrument for the claim — 187 tenants cannot show
what 10K does, and "modern Prometheus handles high cardinality" plus a scheduled backend migration
are assertions, not measurements of the shipped configuration.

DISCRIMINATORS. The tenant is correctly in scope at every emit site via the canonical accessor, so
MUST-6 is satisfied and is not the defect. MUST-5 is not in play: no audit row is written or
altered. The MUST NOT bullet on placeholder-defaulting is not in play either — nothing here
substitutes a value for a missing tenant.
